      "mentionedUsers": [
        {
          "_id": "5b0b06e952d6c72deb336627",
          "alias": "Net Kite",
          "aliasID": "65d0d32c0129d7ae44a01c13",
          "anonymized": false,
          "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/1f98d3e62b8f981e992211db67e7185c.jpg",
          "created": "2018-05-27T19:28:41.841Z",
          "name": "Nifty255",
          "serviceAccount": false,
          "urlName": null
        }
      ],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "5bea0f3dfd98475fa31c69ee",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5be289d3b81508145771ea41",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 5
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b0b06e952d6c72deb336627|full_name}: Sure - but there are times where you don't actually want blending. \n\nAnother thing is - Hand gestures - They're already blended. \n\nIt's not as hard as you might think it is, they're already doing it for the hands. \n\nWhile the current system is fine, this is a more flexible alternative and allows more users to do things in non-jank ways, such as all those Pokemon, Neptunia, or KDA Akali avatars that desperatly want 2D visemes in some capacity, but are stuck with janky solutions such as sliding a plane in and out of the face.\n\nThe problem with that solution is that it creates clipping, and is horribly obvious. \n\nThe way I was able to find around this was using Shader hackery to get around it by using a grabpass to read from pixels I was writing to, but that's horribly expensive, and not really a viable solution for multiple people to be using. (performance issues from grabpasses being thrown around, and also interference since there's only a limited number of pixels you can write to before you start writing to someone else's pixels if they're doing the same thing.)\n\nIt would be a lot simpler to have animations that just, you know, offset the UVs of the mesh with the mouth on it. \n\nIt would have little to no drawbacks to implement, that I'm aware of, and it's not a complex system.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5eb694f4f1473476bdeedf64",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5eb693048a21cd76f3d78a1b",
        "alias": "Administrative Porcupine",
