        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/d294fdbe7f83f42b58a2e8cbabb2b0c9.png",
        "created": "2020-05-09T11:24:52.423Z",
        "name": "MEZZMERR",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2020-05-09T11:33:08.470Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 0,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5be289d3b81508145771ea41",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Just spent all night trying workarounds to make something like this work, to no avail... as far as I can tell, I think the viseme animations are handled by the avatar descriptor component lerping between different shape keys rather than any animations. \nSo... not quite the answer you're proposing, but to get a flexible end result without changing the existing system too much, I believe all we'd need is a transition speed slider, to change the amount of time a viseme takes to lerp. Set it to a high value like 1000 to get an \"instant\" transition to a different shape key.\nAdditionally, other interpolation modes would add for more flexibility and control for visemes! (Constant instead of Linear would be perfect for this)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
