  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-11-07T06:44:35.249Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Instead of only allowing blend shapes / shape keys for visemes, allow us to use a series of 1 frame animations for them; similar to the gestures.\n\nThis would allow for a lot of flexibility, and would allow for 2D visemes to look good by doing material swaps, and without being hacky and sliding extra geometry forward and back, or snapping extra geometry into place with a Shader. \n\nAlong with 2D visemes, it would allow more flexibility in general for 3D visemes as well, as people would now be able to use facial bones, if they're included in the model, to make the animations for the mouth.",
